   <p class="kb-lead">These are not from a book; they came out of the tower. Each one follows a single fault from start to finish: what the alarm said, what I thought it was, which measurement I took, which possibilities it ruled out, what the root cause turned out to be and how we closed it. The point is not the answer — it is the order of the diagnosis.</p>
  <p>A fault tree gives you a fast route from symptom to cause; these pages show you what it is like inside one case. The two complement each other: narrow it down with the <a href="/ariza/">tree</a> first, then read the closest case here.</p>
  <div class="kb-callout"><p><strong>Note:</strong> these are field experience, not a substitute for the manufacturer's service documentation. Your own turbine's OEM instructions, LOTO procedure and site safety rules govern every intervention.</p></div>
