+   <div class="vdb-ozet"><p><b>Symptom</b>“Pitch motor phase current high” alarm. The turbine cannot start in the morning; the pitch system never becomes ready.</p><p><b>Root cause</b>A 2 mm crack in the gearbox housing. After months of oil loss the gears had been running dry.</p></div>
+   <details class="vdb-yol"><summary>Show the diagnostic path</summary><ol class="vdb-akis"><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Symptom</b></span><p>“Pitch motor phase current high” alarm. The turbine cannot start in the morning; the pitch system never becomes ready.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Measurement</b></span><p>Blades moved by hand: one blade stiffer than the others. Motor phase resistances 8.1–8.3 Ω — the motor is healthy.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Root cause</b></span><p>A 2 mm crack in the gearbox housing. After months of oil loss the gears had been running dry.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Solution</b></span><p>Gearbox drained, crack welded and checked by NDT, gears inspected; filter and oil renewed.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Lesson</b></span><p>The oil level had not been checked at the last service. The current rise was visible in the SCADA trend 8 months earlier.</p></li></ol></details>
