+   <details class="vdb-yol"><summary>Show the diagnostic path</summary><ol class="vdb-akis"><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Symptom</b></span><p>In 14 m/s wind the nacelle swings back and forth; the yaw angle in SCADA keeps changing, with a rhythmic knocking sound.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Measurement</b></span><p>One-hour yaw angle trend: ±18°, 0.5–1 Hz. Yaw motor and angle feedback tested in test mode.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Root cause</b></span><p>Three factors together: reduced bearing lubrication, a loose wind direction sensor and a PLC P gain above normal (1.5).</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Solution</b></span><p>P gain set to 0.6, sensor tightened and calibrated, bearing greased. Two weeks later the oscillation was ±2–3°.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Lesson</b></span><p>Hunting is rarely a single cause: software, sensor and lubrication are checked together.</p></li></ol></details>
