+   <details class="vdb-yol"><summary>Show the diagnostic path</summary><ol class="vdb-akis"><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Symptom</b></span><p>The turbine is producing normally. During greasing, dark grey metallic grease comes out of some points; a rubbing sound at one position.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Measurement</b></span><p>Grease from each point collected separately. Metal concentrated at three neighbouring points (a sector map); a magnet test confirmed steel particles.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Root cause</b></span><p>The automatic lubrication line is blocked; one sector of the bearing went without grease and wore.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Solution</b></span><p>Line cleared, the sector greased until clean grease came out, three months of short-interval follow-up. No bearing replacement needed.</p></li><li><span class="vdb-ak-e"><b>Lesson</b></span><p>Collect purged grease point by point. A running pump does not mean grease reaches every point.</p></li></ol></details>
